WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.654
For over a decade, Bernie Calderon
Magtalas has helped the Philippine

00:00:04.654 --> 00:00:09.894
Government decide which energy, transport,
and climate investments are worth making.

00:00:10.664 --> 00:00:14.049
He started at the Department
of Energy in 2015,

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:17.542
and is now a Supervising
Economic Development Specialist

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:21.034
at the Department of Economy,
Planning, and Development.

00:00:21.804 --> 00:00:26.173
Thirty-four projects. USD 14.05 billion.

00:00:26.173 --> 00:00:29.061
Airports, roads, rail, energy, and ports.

00:00:29.831 --> 00:00:33.570
All appraised under the ICC
review framework, covering

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.828
financial and economic
models;

00:00:35.828 --> 00:00:41.169
market, technical, social, environmental,
institutional, and gender analyses;

00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:43.955
and for Public-Private
Partnership projects,

00:00:43.955 --> 00:00:46.487
concessions, risk, and
prequalification.

00:00:47.257 --> 00:00:49.744
Fifteen development partner programs.

00:00:49.744 --> 00:00:51.492
Twelve consulting studies.

00:00:51.492 --> 00:00:54.046
Forty-eight bills, laws, and policies.

00:00:54.046 --> 00:00:56.331
And eight national boards advised.

00:00:57.101 --> 00:01:01.593
He built the Philippines' first Regional
Infrastructure Development Index,

00:01:01.593 --> 00:01:07.625
and a model ranking 207 projects
in a USD 176 billion pipeline.

00:01:08.395 --> 00:01:11.667
A Waseda University graduate
and JICA scholar,

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:15.596
he was a Congress Future Energy
Leader of the World Energy Council,

00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:20.328
and is part of SIPA's Regional Knowledge
Network on Sustainable Infrastructure,

00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:23.904
along with policymakers and
experts across Southeast Asia.

00:01:24.674 --> 00:01:28.908
See the full portfolio at
bcmagtalas.github.io.
